%N A305856 Number of unlabeled intersecting set-systems on up to n vertices.
%C A305856 An intersecting set-system is a finite set of finite nonempty sets (edges), any two of which have a nonempty intersection.
%C A305856 For n = 7, 8, 9, the terms were computed using Burnside's lemma over the cycle types of S_n. For each permutation, the fixed intersecting set-systems were counted as independent sets in the corresponding orbit disjointness graph. The identity contribution is A051185(n). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Aug 22 2026
%H A305856 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A305856/a305856.pdf">Supporting computational note for A305856</a>
%F A305856 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} Fix(sigma), where Fix(sigma) is the number of intersecting set-systems invariant under sigma. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Aug 22 2026
%e A305856 Non-isomorphic representatives of the a(3) = 14 intersecting set-systems:
%e A305856   {}
%e A305856   {{1}}
%e A305856   {{1,2}}
%e A305856   {{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{2},{1,2}}
%e A305856   {{3},{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{1,3},{2,3}}
%e A305856   {{2,3},{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{3},{1,3},{2,3}}
%e A305856   {{3},{2,3},{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{1,2},{1,3},{2,3}}
%e A305856   {{1,3},{2,3},{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{3},{1,3},{2,3},{1,2,3}}
%e A305856   {{1,2},{1,3},{2,3},{1,2,3}}
